From 800b37cc50fa9e2d0c741814f9fc19f3f8d75a36 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ROMForge Engineering <romforge@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 19:41:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] relay: bank/restore the full out/ ninja state between
 slices
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

ccache-only persistence re-paid soong analysis + all Java/Kotlin/proto/
dex/packaging work every slice, so wasted time grew linearly with the
slice number. The out/ relay (tar|zstd|split --filter, symbols excluded)
makes resume exact for every language; slice numbering derives from the
newest state-cache-sN tag. Source banking also moved to the zero-staging
stream path so pack parts never share a disk with tree+out again.

Note: split --filter hands the chunk to the filter on stdin — the filter
writes $FILE, hashes it, uploads it, removes it.
---
 .github/workflows/build.yml | 33 ++++++++++++---
 scripts/04_upload_cache.sh  | 72 +++++++++++++++++++--------------
 scripts/05_restore_cache.sh | 21 ++++++++++
 scripts/lib_stream.sh       | 80 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 171 insertions(+), 35 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 scripts/lib_stream.sh

